                            "Austrian German"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dca00c55-f586-493f-bf7d-13acb09f96d9",
                                "sense_id": "2d0df6e1-f286-3101-8272-4c09faf0925e",
                                "text": "Geh, gib dem Sandler einen Euro."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6aadffc-22af-347f-a2d2-bf97fdd9638c",
                        "entry_id": "0d9b307a-b389-35ee-b800-38ed177bf90a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "verwahrloste Person, die auf der Straße lebt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Austrian German",
                            "derogatory",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f149d84b-6c54-4a3c-8fa9-9ee5e71446b9",
                                "sense_id": "d6aadffc-22af-347f-a2d2-bf97fdd9638c",
                                "text": "Willst du unter der Brücke schlafen wie ein Sandler?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2959b47-66b4-4885-97e2-5174baa9e108",
                                "sense_id": "d6aadffc-22af-347f-a2d2-bf97fdd9638c",
                                "text": "„‚[…] Auch der von heute Abend war bestimmt ein Gstopfter, obwohl er wie der letzte Sandler ausgesehen hat‘, pflichtete Ella ihrer Freundin bei.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d207d53-e54b-48ed-9fc5-1b5e3c9504f1",
                                "sense_id": "d6aadffc-22af-347f-a2d2-bf97fdd9638c",
                                "text": "Wolfgang Ambros (österreichischer Liedermacher) in seinem Lied ´Des Sandlers Flucht´ - „Oh höft's ma, bitte höft's ma!“, hod da Sandler gschrian: „I wü ned dass mi aussetrogn und in' Häfn ummefian!“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2bbb62ca-13c4-3c2b-a302-fdb906a59f03",
                        "entry_id": "0d9b307a-b389-35ee-b800-38ed177bf90a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "jemand, der nicht arbeiten möchte"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Austrian German",
                            "derogatory"
                        ],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "076e7b68-a4dc-4b0c-85b5-2964d6688158",
                        "source_entry_id": "0d9b307a-b389-35ee-b800-38ed177bf90a",
                        "source_sense_id": "2d0df6e1-f286-3101-8272-4c09faf0925e",
                        "source_sense_description": "österreichisch: Bettler",
                        "target_lang_word": "beggar",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "beggar",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0a2c568-ca68-365a-ac35-30d1bee0dce2",
                                        "entry_id": "6ad00d84-bafc-3f45-9809-d8d3cdff1c56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who begs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "926205e5-52fd-41c4-b113-10bbd42fa6bf",
                                                "sense_id": "f0a2c568-ca68-365a-ac35-30d1bee0dce2",
                                                "text": "“[…] They talk of you as if you were Croesus—and I expect the beggars sponge on you unconscionably.” And Vickers launched forth into a tirade very different from his platform utterances. He spoke with extreme contempt of the dense stupidity exhibited on all occasions by the working classes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6124751d-c4b7-43e7-8e6c-4f5670435b06",
                                                "sense_id": "f0a2c568-ca68-365a-ac35-30d1bee0dce2",
                                                "text": "Odysseus has returned to his home disguised as a beggar."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9395d9ae-6187-3568-9c22-59033e99ce7b",
                                        "entry_id": "6ad00d84-bafc-3f45-9809-d8d3cdff1c56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person suffering from extreme poverty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "514e818e-86ed-4dde-9fbb-67b283bb0107",
                                                "sense_id": "9395d9ae-6187-3568-9c22-59033e99ce7b",
                                                "text": "I'm to be a poor, crawling beggar, sponging for rum, when I might be rolling in a coach!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8067cce7-1ab4-32ad-b5e1-52455d14aea7",
                                        "entry_id": "6ad00d84-bafc-3f45-9809-d8d3cdff1c56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mean or wretched person; a scoundrel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "endearing",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07950a43-0f15-4657-a4d3-0668f5da171b",
                                                "sense_id": "8067cce7-1ab4-32ad-b5e1-52455d14aea7",
                                                "text": "What does that silly beggar think he's doing?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e45c299-4aec-3741-af0b-422b7af78250",
                                        "entry_id": "6ad00d84-bafc-3f45-9809-d8d3cdff1c56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A minced oath for bugger."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "beggar",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e32bae4-1ba6-3548-b770-126bc1fadcd7",
                                        "entry_id": "9b0a77e1-ca87-3ee7-9f17-96c8ed32b183",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a beggar of someone; impoverish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6efa4dea-8814-3995-a787-a1059d4c4de5",
                                        "entry_id": "9b0a77e1-ca87-3ee7-9f17-96c8ed32b183",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To exhaust the resources of; to outdo or go beyond."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89c4659a-da1d-4b96-8272-c04324f808e0",
                                                "sense_id": "6efa4dea-8814-3995-a787-a1059d4c4de5",
                                                "text": "`Now,' answered Ayesha, with proud humility - `now when my lord doth speak thus royally and give with so free a hand, it cannot become me to lag behind in words, and be beggared of my generosity.'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5772ead-83c2-4953-870a-75dbbecf1719",
                                                "sense_id": "6efa4dea-8814-3995-a787-a1059d4c4de5",
                                                "text": "It was a scene of such beauty it caught all his attention. / Some things beggar likeness, he thought."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8380af4a-ef98-47a3-b51d-f2547b2c3f99",
                                                "sense_id": "6efa4dea-8814-3995-a787-a1059d4c4de5",
                                                "text": "Taking the ontological temperature of today and of the pre-revolutionary 18th century, Mr. Kundera finds that the speed we love has beggared us of pleasure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
